## Conventions (acme)
- Every service exposes `/healthz` and `/readyz`; never remove them.
- Money is stored as integer minor units with an ISO 4217 currency code, never as floats.
- Public API changes start in the OpenAPI file and go through review before code.
- Branches are `<ticket>-<short-name>`; squash-merge to `main`.

## Known repos (acme)
- acme-api — Public REST gateway · /Volumes/work/acme/api
- billing-api (billing, invoices) — Invoicing and payment orchestration; OpenAPI in api/openapi.yaml · /Volumes/work/acme/billing-api · notes: ~/acme-store/repos/billing-api/notes.md
- events-pipeline (events, pipeline) — Kafka consumers that turn raw events into billing and ML features · /Volumes/work/acme/ml/events-pipeline · notes: ~/acme-store/repos/events-pipeline/notes.md
- feature-store (feature, store) — Online and offline feature serving; dbt models in models/ · (not cloned here)
- ml-platform (ml) — Shared training and feature tooling · /Volumes/work/acme/ml/ml-platform
- web-dashboard · /Volumes/work/acme/web-dashboard

## This repo
Scope: acme-ml. Related: billing-api, ml-platform (read access granted).
For any repo above, read its code at the listed path; check its notes first if listed.
